# Burning Sun — ls colours.
#
# ANSI blue (4) and bright blue (12) are the rubric: Claude Code draws inline
# code and hyperlinks with them on a path that ignores its own theme, so those
# two slots carry the ember. `ls` therefore has to stay off blue entirely, or
# every directory would burn.
#
# Everything here separates by weight and grey value instead, with the ember
# reserved for the two things worth catching the eye: broken links and
# executables. Colour numbers, not hex, so this follows the light/dark switch
# along with the rest of the terminal palette.

RESET 0
NORMAL 00
FILE 00

DIR              01;37       # bold ink
LINK             04;37       # underlined
ORPHAN           01;31       # broken symlink — ember
MISSING          01;31
EXEC             01;31       # executable — ember
SETUID           01;31
SETGID           01;31
CAPABILITY       01;31
STICKY           01;37
OTHER_WRITABLE   01;37
STICKY_OTHER_WRITABLE 01;37

FIFO             33
SOCK             33
DOOR             33
BLK              33
CHR              33

# Archives and media step down the grey ramp rather than picking up hues.
.tar 33
.tgz 33
.zip 33
.gz  33
.bz2 33
.xz  33
.zst 33
.7z  33
.rar 33

.jpg 90
.jpeg 90
.png 90
.gif 90
.webp 90
.svg 90
.mp4 90
.mkv 90
.webm 90
.mp3 90
.flac 90
.wav 90
.pdf 90
